Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 03:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: next calendar event on the lock screen

The Sable locked glance shows the next event from Sable Calendar under
the clock, above the Peek (owner pick from the JL10 review, after
BlackBerry 10): "Today 9:30 · Standup", "Now · Standup" or "Tomorrow
all day · Trip". Only today's and tomorrow's events show. While the
lock screen hides notification content the event is named "Event", so
a locked phone never shows a meeting's name the user hides.

SystemUI reads Sable Calendar's "next" snapshot off the main thread
when the lock screen shows and when the calendar changes. Sable
Calendar answers only SystemUI and Sable Start, from the calendars the
user shows, and only while it holds READ_CALENDAR; without Sable
Calendar nothing shows. The day and line rules are pure Java
(SableLockGlance.eventDay and eventLine, unit tested). Hidden while
dozing; Lock screen size scales it like the rest of the glance.
